    "body": "## What\n\nPronunciation fixes found while making the 「24GB 显卡跑 60GB 视频模型」 explainer video (2026-10-19). Every entry was measured with `pron_check.py` (Xiaoxiao voice + Whisper):\n\n| Written | Spoken | Before (Whisper) → after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| checkpoint | check point | ChatPoint in every carrier → **checkpoint** |\n| OOM | O O M | Om (read as a word) → **OOM** |\n| comfy-kitchen | Comfy Kitchen | a bare *kitchen* → Tichen in every spelling; the pair passes |\n| fa (FlashAttention backend) | F A | read as a syllable in context (Fall / 发 / 法 / Ford) → **FA** |\n\nRewords added to the table:\n- `int mm` → 「PyTorch 自带的 INT8 矩阵乘接口」\n- `INT32` → 「32 位整数累加」\n\nThe 行 note now also covers 「按行动态量化」: there 行 sits before 动 and forms 行动, so the text should be written 「逐行做动态量化」.\n\n## pron_check fix\n\nThe carrier now reads the term's full spoken form with `patterns` applied (`to_spoken`, not just `spoken_token`). Before this, `24GB` was synthesized raw and reported as a FAIL (heard `24G`), even though the engine sends `24 G B`, which passes. Verified: `24 G B` / `60 G B` / `32 G B` all come back OK.\n\n## Worker-dispatch lessons\n\n`references/worker-dispatch.md` gains a list of lessons to append to every dispatch:\n- no whole-frame camera drift;\n- SVG `transformOrigin` on both sides of a `fromTo` (to-side only shifted an axis by 480px);\n- how to chain short video clips, and why the `nested_media_start_basis_ambiguous` lint warning is expected;\n- `check_frames` reports \"missing follow strip\" on whichever frame is currently the highest-numbered, so workers should ignore it mid-run;\n- excerpt line ranges are fixed upstream, never paraphrased.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `uvx pytest tests/test_explainer_pronounce.py`: 11 passed (new `test_terms_from_the_24gb_video`).\n- pre-commit: clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
